==============================================================================
v100  QLTO on ZZ+XY crosstalk: monolithic vs alternating bootstrap
==============================================================================
  N=4, M=13, 27x coefficient spread. T=4, symmetric Suzuki reps=4,
  alpha=0.3, probe=random(4), 65536 shots, 40 circuits each arm.

  start   err ALL 0.0597   err ZZ 0.0558

  scheme                       err ALL      err ZZ  circuits
  ----------------------------------------------------------
  monolithic M=13               0.0172      0.0091        40
  bootstrap, r RESET            0.3585      0.0917        40
  bootstrap, r CARRIED          0.0370      0.0158        40

  The radius must carry across stages. Resetting it is worse than
  not peeling; carrying it is 3.2x better on the weak ZZ terms.
